  "independent_author_derivation": [
    "For x>1, successive multiplication by x increases positive powers: -1<0<1<x<x^2<x^3. This realizes a, for example x=2.",
    "For 0<x<1, successive multiplication by x decreases positive powers: -1<0<x^3<x^2<x<1. This realizes c, for example x=1/2.",
    "For x<-1, x^3<x<-1 and x^2>1, giving x^3<x<-1<0<1<x^2. This realizes b, for example x=-2.",
    "For -1<x<0, x<x^3<0 and 0<x^2<1, giving -1<x<x^3<0<x^2<1. This realizes d, for example x=-1/2.",
    "Equality cases x=-1,0,1 respectively give A=C=-1,B=1; A=B=C=0; A=B=C=1. None realizes the three distinct markers shown, so strict regimes exhaust the source diagrams.",
    "If B<A, then x^2<x, hence x(x-1)<0 and 0<x<1. Consequently C=x^3<x^2=B. Both e(B<C<A) and f(B<A<C) contradict this consequence. All four other rows are realized."
  ],
  "feasible_marker_orders": {
    "a": "-1<0<1<A<B<C",
    "b": "C<A<-1<0<1<B",
    "c": "-1<0<C<B<A<1",
    "d": "-1<A<C<0<B<1"
  },
